DO  - 10.5194/hess-19-2899-2015
UR  - https://hess.copernicus.org/articles/19/2899/2015/
N1  - Found and read in full 2026-09-23 (open access, Copernicus/HESS, no paywall), while searching for a grassland/savanna/shrubland Kc source to fill the registry's "not yet checked" gap for that biome. Same P.T.S. Oliveira as oliveira2016 (the existing Cerrado CN-analog citation for Flooded Grasslands) and a co-author on vallejunior2019 (tropical pasture, CN framework breaks down) -- one coherent Brazilian Cerrado hydrology research program feeding three separate registry cells, not a coincidence. Two real cerrado savanna-woodland sites (PDG, IAB, "cerrado sensu stricto denso," 50-70% arborous cover, 5-8m trees, Koppen Cwa humid subtropical -- a savanna WOODLAND physiognomy, closer to Brush/Shrubs than open Grassland in WWF-SIPA's own typology, worth being precise about). Empirical ET model, following the same Nagler et al. (2013) structural form already known from nagler2009: ET = ETo[a(1-e^(-b*EVI)) - c], fitted via genetic algorithm against PDG flux-tower data (2001-2003): a=10.36, b=12.31, c=9.74. R2=0.73 (daily, full time series), R2=0.78 (monthly), RMSE ~17-21% (daily) -- comparable error magnitude to Negron Juarez's own ~17% average. Annual ET: 822 mm/yr (PDG, model-fit site) and 823 mm/yr (IAB, independent validation site, using field-measured water-balance components) -- essentially identical, real cross-site consistency, not just a single-site fit. Real candidate for the Tropical & Subtropical Grasslands/Savannas/Shrublands Kc cell; doesn't conflict with vallejunior2019's CN-framework-breaks-down finding since that's about runoff generation (CN), this is about ET/Kc, separate mechanisms in the SWY model.
ER  -
